+/*
+ * BOLD BY FAMILY WHEN THE TYPEFACE NAME IS NOT ONE WE PUBLISH.
+ *
+ * -convertFont:toHaveTrait: looks the font up with fontFamilyWithTypefaceName:, which needs the
+ * font NAME to be one of the typeface names the display enumerated. The system font is not: it is
+ * called San Francisco, and the typefaces this backend publishes are named with fontconfig
+ * patterns. So the conversion found no family, returned the font unchanged, and the application
+ * name in the menu bar and the title of every window came out in the regular weight while the code
+ * asking for them read boldSystemFontOfSize.
+ *
+ * The family is what has the faces, so ask it directly when the conversion has nothing to say.
+ */
